  "figure": "/home/michaelvolk/Documents/projects/torchcell.worktrees/feat/kinetics-equilibrator-datasets/notes/assets/images/032-amino-acid-module/betaxanthin_amino_acid_correlation_2026-09-24-21-02-01.svg",
  "note": "Betaxanthin: Cachera 2023 corrected 24 h colony fluorescence per gene (population-centered score). Amino acids: Mulleder 2016 mM (prototroph, minimal medium) and Cooper 2010 ratio to the plate mean (auxotroph, complete medium). Strains matched on the systematic ORF. The ceiling is sqrt(reliability_betaxanthin * reliability_amino_acid) with the betaxanthin reliability the stored value of the 027 variance-components read, Mulleder's the log10 retest Spearman over 194 strains, Cooper's the duplicate-strain Spearman. The pool fit is ridge over the log10 profile, standardized and median-filled on the training fold, five strain folds, alpha chosen on an inner split, scored out of fold; the permuted reference shuffles the target. The go and go+pool fits use the same folds with the deleted gene's propagated GO multi-hot (ess_solve_encodings_YPD_bx_go.npz), standardized on the training fold, alone and beside the pool."
}